@startuml context_diagram
skinparam rectangleStyle rounded
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam dpi 160
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDEB
skinparam noteBorderColor #999999
skinparam packageBackgroundColor white
skinparam packageBorderColor #666666
skinparam rectangleBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
skinparam rectangleBorderColor #666666
skinparam arrowColor #555555
skinparam titleFontColor #111111

title Claude Agent SDK Adapter — Context / Block Diagram\n<size:11><color:#666666>Action governance: full. Inference governance: out of reach, shown not hidden.</color></size>

rectangle "K9-AIF Caller\n(Squad step, Orchestrator, or\ndirect facade call)" as Caller

package "K9ClaudeAgentSDKAdapter (facade)" as Facade {
  rectangle "ClaudeAgentSDKPayloadMapper\nto_sdk_input() / from_sdk_output()" as Mapper
}

package "ClaudeAgentSDKOrchestratorAdapter\n(sole capability broker)" as OrchAdapter {
  rectangle "Zero Trust\napply_zero_trust()" as ZT
  rectangle "Ingress governance\napply_pre_governance()" as Ingress
  rectangle "Tool / MCP server registry\n(_capabilities, adapter-owned)" as ToolRegistry
  rectangle "can_use_tool\n(egress gate, every tool call,\ntop-level AND subagent)" as CanUseTool
  rectangle "Subagent definitions\n(tools subset of _capabilities,\nvalidated at construction)" as Subagents
  rectangle "Final-output egress\napply_post_governance()" as FinalEgress
  rectangle "Audit trail\npublish_event()" as Audit
}

package "k9x_Shield (ShieldGovernance)" as Shield {
  rectangle "Ingress chain\nInputSizeCheck, PromptInjectionCheck,\nPIIBoundaryCheck" as IngressChain
  rectangle "Egress chain\nSemanticDriftCheck, ToolArgumentCheck,\nExecutionGuardCheck, PIIBoundaryCheck" as EgressChain
}

package "Claude Agent SDK (external, Claude-only)" as SDK {
  rectangle "query() / ClaudeSDKClient\nagent loop" as Loop
  rectangle "bundled 'claude' CLI subprocess\n(owns its own inference end to end)" as CLI
}

cloud "Anthropic API\n(or Bedrock / Vertex / Azure Foundry,\nstill Claude, different hosting)" as Anthropic

rectangle "K9ModelRouter\nllm_invoke() -> LLMFactory -> backend\n(Ollama, OpenAI, Watsonx, Claude-direct, ...)" as ModelRouter

Caller --> Facade
Facade --> Mapper
Mapper --> OrchAdapter

ZT --> Ingress
Ingress --> IngressChain
Ingress --> ToolRegistry
ToolRegistry --> CanUseTool
Subagents --> CanUseTool
CanUseTool --> EgressChain
CanUseTool --> Loop : allow / deny\nper tool call
Loop --> CLI
CLI --> Anthropic
Loop --> FinalEgress
FinalEgress --> EgressChain
FinalEgress --> Audit
Audit --> Caller : governed result

CLI ..[#CC3333,thickness=2]..> ModelRouter : "**NOT CONNECTED**\nSDK's own model calls never\nreach llm_invoke, a structural\nSDK limitation, not an adapter gap"

note right of ModelRouter
  This is where a native K9-AIF agent,
  or a CrewAI agent behind
  K9XLiteLLMBridgeAdapter, would be:
  provider-agnostic, swappable by config.

  The Claude Agent SDK's own loop
  cannot be routed here. Solutions
  needing that should use a direct-API
  BaseLLM adapter instead (Pet Store
  Agentic's DirectApiDiagnosisAgent
  pattern), fully governed on both
  axes, at the cost of writing the
  tool-use loop yourself instead of
  getting Claude's autonomous loop
  for free.
end note

note bottom of OrchAdapter
  CONFORMANCE TIER: action-governed, not fully-governed.
  Verified from the SDK's own source: every can_use_tool
  control request, top-level agent or any subagent,
  carries ToolPermissionContext.agent_id and hits this
  one callback. No separate, bypassing path exists.
end note

@enduml
